<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One page of verse, one column, full width. Running head top left. Page number top right. Signature mark at the foot right.</layout>
  <page_number>49</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>D. j.</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Robur suspicimus, cui Sapientia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Et nexu Bonitas Iusta adamantino</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Hærent, non homini conspicuo modo.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Quid pœnas memorem temporibus graues</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Prisci terricolūm, dum genus abstulit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Ultrix lympha? scelus quid retegam lacu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Contectum, fluido sulphure dum pluens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Æther, inque olidas flamma, fauillaque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Est lenti scatebras versa bituminis?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Quid plagas Pharÿs multiplices datas?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Aut quid colla iugo pressa Philistica?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Vel miranda, fides quæ pia concipit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Seris plurima quæ facta nepotibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Ætas prisca patrum dante dedit Deo?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Quæ sol temporibus contuitus novis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Quorum terra recens conscia, non leui</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Penna, Musa, bonis pande minoribus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>At rerum nimio pondere ne gemas,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Vnum sit facinus dicere nunc satis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Quod multis potis est æquiparavit [?].</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Quod tellure fati, pellere dum Iouem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Tentarunt patriis sedibus, impio</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Versabant animo, quicquid &amp; improbus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Contemptor Capaneus numinis, &amp; fonos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Salmoneus imitans sedis Olympicæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Infanus Phaëton, Sysiphus, &amp; vagus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Ixion, reliqui denique, quos nigro</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Pungit Musa vetus pollice, quod lues.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Line 'Contectum' is printed with a worn letter, read as Contectum [?] (from 'Conteclum'). 'æquiparavit' is worn at the line end and is doubtful. 'Phaëton' read with diaeresis as printed. Macron/tilde over the u in 'terricolūm' read as a left-out m. The stanza division follows the printed indents. Signature 'D. j.' sits below the text, right.</notes>
</page>
